>When the compositor supports color management (and the particular tf we need) we already try for PASS_THROUGH_EXT and then sRGB for proprietary nvidia so I'm not sure what else I could do.

The error goes away if I replace the format list by

```c
	// Determine which formats to prefer based on the requested capabilities.
	FixedVector<FormatCandidate, 4> preferred_formats;
	preferred_formats.push_back({ VK_FORMAT_R16G16B16A16_SFLOAT, VK_COLOR_SPACE_PASS_THROUGH_EXT });
	preferred_formats.push_back({ VK_FORMAT_R16G16B16A16_SFLOAT, VK_COLOR_SPACE_SRGB_NONLINEAR_KHR });
```

The following patch makes the test look completely identical:

```diff
diff --git a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/blit.glsl b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/blit.glsl
index b9b54d8e0b..5fa998eaa9 100644
--- a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/blit.glsl
+++ b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/blit.glsl
@@ -90,8 +90,7 @@ vec3 srgb_to_linear(vec3 color) {
 }
 
 vec3 linear_to_srgb(vec3 color) {
-	const vec3 a = vec3(0.055f);
-	return mix((vec3(1.0f) + a) * pow(color.rgb, vec3(1.0f / 2.4f)) - a, 12.92f * color.rgb, lessThan(color.rgb, vec3(0.0031308f)));
+	return pow(color, vec3(1.0/2.2));
 }
 
 // From https://alex.vlachos.com/graphics/Alex_Vlachos_Advanced_VR_Rendering_GDC2015.pdf
```

